      "rationale": "Inline shells on Windows mangle non-ASCII (Vietnamese diacritics) via console code page, lose backslash escapes through cmd /c re-parsing, and break on continuation/here-string/heavy-quote payloads. The script-file path writes the body as a temp artifact (UTF-8 BOM for .ps1 / plain UTF-8 for .js) and invokes via -File / direct path so the interpreter reads source bytes unchanged.",
      "path_as_argv_warning": "R55 ADDITIONAL RULE: NEVER pass non-ASCII paths (Vietnamese diacritics, UNC shares with national characters) as DIRECT shell argv even with permitted runtimes. The Windows console argv re-encoding still applies BEFORE the interpreter parses argv. Symptom: downstream tools receive mojibake bytes and filesystem probes return exists=false. Safe routes: (a) write path into the script file body (run_ps1_script / run_node_script — body is read as UTF-8/UTF-8-BOM, no argv transit); (b) pass path as a JSON request body field (HTTP transport stays UTF-8 end-to-end). The R54 input mojibake detector on sample_unc_paths_with_root_check will surface INPUT_MOJIBAKE_SUSPECTED if upstream argv corruption occurred.",
